Third-party code, models and data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Derived code
  The training and evaluation harness (pretrain/, sft/, util/, model/) descends
  from the public implementation of SAC (Autoencoding-Free Context Compression
  for LLMs via Contextual Semantic Anchors), which is also one of the baselines
  in this paper. The Matryoshka anchor representation, the elastic allocator,
  the tolerance-conditioned objective and the oracle labeling are additions made
  here.

Baseline reimplementations
  baselines/icae/  and baselines/c500x/ are our own implementations of the ICAE
  and 500xCompressor training and evaluation harnesses, written against
  transformers and peft. They contain no code copied from the upstream projects.
  Refer to the upstream repositories for the original implementations:
    ICAE            — In-context Autoencoder for Context Compression
    500xCompressor  — Generalized Prompt Compression for LLMs
  LongLLMLingua is used through the published `llmlingua` package.

Backbones
  Llama 3.1 / Llama 3.2 models are subject to the Meta Llama community license.
  Qwen2.5 models are subject to the Qwen license. Model weights are not
  distributed in this repository.

